# Task 8A Report: V5 Runtime Event and Evaluator Contracts

## Scope

Task 8A changed only the four approved V5 source modules plus the package export surface:

- `core/pit_optimizer_v5/memory.py`
- `core/pit_optimizer_v5/artifacts.py`
- `core/pit_optimizer_v5/contracts.py`
- `core/pit_optimizer_v5/evaluator.py`
- `core/pit_optimizer_v5/__init__.py` (exports only)

No provider, Docker, replay, market-data, orchestration, V2-V4, authorization, or test-file code was
changed or invoked.

## Durable pre-experiment round outcomes

- Added the closed campaign-level `round_outcome` event and frozen `RoundOutcomePayloadV5`, whose
  authority is exactly one of `NoNovelHypothesisAuthorityV5`,
  `NoveltyExhaustedAuthorityV5`, or `CriticUnavailableAuthorityV5`.
- No generic artifact-ref bag remains. Each variant binds only its relevant named identities:
  discovery/search-state transition and parent authority, exact request/evidence/attempt/artifact or
  selection identities, and—for critic unavailability—the exact attempted experiment batch plus
  tagged per-experiment pre-critic evidence identities. The closed tagged evidence kinds reject
  unrelated evidence and episode ordinals on non-episode facts.
- Novelty exhaustion embeds an ordered, non-duplicated set of no-novel parent authorities and proves
  their exact search-state chain. Critic-unavailable requires a nonempty real experiment batch and
  requires its retained evidence to cover exactly that batch.
- Canonical artifact decoding uses this closed union and rejects cross-status, extra, or missing
  authority fields. The old blind authentication of untyped child references was removed; Task 8B
  must persist and decode the named typed objects whose canonical digests these authorities bind.
- Recovery recognizes at most one terminal outcome, requires it to be the final chain event, returns
  it directly, and schedules no further local steps. The repository rejects any append after a
  durable terminal outcome.
- Experiment-record and checkpoint/archive code is unchanged. A critic-unavailable outcome therefore
  cannot manufacture a post-critic `ExperimentRecordV5` or alter promotion authority.

## Unified policy revision identity and V3 worker boundary

- `EvaluatorContractV5` now pins `baseline_policy_revision_sha256` separately from the retained
  `baseline_source_bundle_sha256` source-artifact authority used by search reconstruction.
- `PitPanelEvaluatorV5` requires the exact authenticated `PolicyRevisionIdentityV5` at construction,
  verifies it against the evaluator contract, and emits its `.sha256` for baseline evidence.
- Candidate evaluation and `CandidateWorkerBindingV5` now also carry the complete typed policy
  revision. Candidate trusted-runtime and immutable-constraint authority must match the baseline;
  evidence identity is always the revision `.sha256`, never a raw source-bundle digest.
- The evaluator is V3-only: exact interface version 3, all six decision methods including
  `evaluate_add_on`, and `close`. Baseline factories now return `BaselineWorkerBindingV5`, symmetric
  with candidate bindings, and the evaluator rejects any binding whose full
  `PolicyRevisionIdentityV5` differs from the claimed baseline before simulation.
- The default in-process baseline factory hashes the exact four loaded editable source files and
  requires them to equal the claimed revision source map before returning its identity-bearing V3
  binding. Per-scenario single-worker allocation, mismatch close, reuse rejection, and
  simulator-owned normal close behavior remain intact.

## Trusted evaluator source closure

`EVALUATOR_SOURCE_PATHS_V5` now contains 45 canonical files. In addition to the reached V3
contract/adapter/feature stack, the review closure adds the actually executed market-regime and
entry-contract modules, settings and engine policy, data-client helpers, CANSLIM A/C/I/N/S logic,
earnings tracing, and the CANSLIM/config package initializers. Fiscal/group RS,
PIT industry/provenance/universe logic, V2 parity policy implementations, V3 package bootstrap, and
the V5 revision/scope contracts remain covered. The four editable V3 policy modules remain outside
the trusted runtime set because their exact bytes are authenticated separately by
`PolicyRevisionIdentityV5`.

## Direct deterministic verification

The initial local direct fake smoke reported `task8a-direct-smoke-ok`; the focused review smoke
reported `task8a-review-direct-smoke-ok` and covered:

- all three round-outcome constructions and status bindings;
- canonical closed-authority artifact encode/decode/load round trips, extra/cross-status field
  rejection, terminal recovery, post-terminal chain rejection, and absence of experiment-record
  writes;
- exact V3 worker acceptance plus V2 and missing-`evaluate_add_on` rejection;
- candidate and baseline binding to the complete policy revision, rejection and close of a
  mismatched baseline binding, and rejection of an identity-free baseline factory;
- rejection of a raw digest in place of the baseline revision; and
- exact trusted source-map construction and required V3 source membership.

Final verification passed fresh module compilation, Ruff check/format, package and module export
integrity, forbidden-coupling search, trusted 45-file source-map reconstruction, and
`git diff --check`. The commit hooks also passed Ruff, whitespace, end-of-file, YAML, and merge-marker
checks. Existing tests were neither added, changed, nor run, per the explicit override.

## Task 8B boundary

Task 8A exposes only pure contracts and recovery facts. Before enabling any provider call, Task 8B
must add typed create-only persistence and typed load/verification for the exact `RoleRequestV5`,
completion result, `RoleAttemptFactsV5`, terminal settlement receipt, and parsed role artifact. It
must add a role-completion event/recovery step that binds those decoded objects so a restart cannot
repeat an already-settled provider attempt. Generic `append_input` is not sufficient for this
authority. Runtime orchestration must then choose when to emit a terminal outcome, prove every named
digest against those typed objects, and leave archive/checkpoint promotion unchanged when critic
authorization is unavailable.
